(This section reports potential problems with your run, but such reporting is often not very accurate. With many ) Tj
ET
BT
55 621 Td
(parameters in a multilocus analysis, it is common that some parameters for some loci will not be informative. ) Tj
ET
BT
55 606 Td
(These parameters then trigger suggestions to increase the prior range that are not sensible. Do not blindly follow ) Tj
ET
BT
55 591 Td
(the suggestions given. If some parameters are flagged, inspect the tables carefully and judge whether an action ) Tj
ET
BT
55 576 Td
(is required. Suppose you run a Bayesian inference with sequence data for macroscopic species. In that case, ) Tj
ET
BT
55 561 Td
(there is rarely the need to increase the prior for Theta beyond 0.1. If you use microsatellites data, it is rather ) Tj
ET
BT
55 546 Td
(common that your prior distribution for Theta should have a range from 0.0 to 100 or more. With many ) Tj
ET
BT
55 531 Td
(populations \050\0763\051, it is also very common that some migration routes are estimated poorly because the data ) Tj
ET
BT
55 516 Td
(contains little or no information for that route. Increasing the prior range will not help in such situations, but ) Tj
ET
BT
55 501 Td
(reducing the number of parameters may help.) Tj
ET
